# What the `lab-host role tests` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml installs.
# This is the file a person edits. requirements-role-tests.txt beside it is
# the lock file made from it: the same version plus everything it depends on,
# each with the SHA256 checksums pip must see before it installs the file.
#
# ansible-core here is the release lab-host/bootstrap.sh puts on the host
# (ANSIBLE_CORE_VERSION in lab-image/versions.env). Move the three together:
# that line, this file and requirements-lint.in.
#
# After changing the line, rebuild the lock from this folder, on the Python
# the job uses (3.15):
#
#   pip-compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-role-tests.txt requirements-role-tests.in
ansible-core==2.22.0
